@startuml
!include style.puml
title Doc Pup - Concurrent Cancellation Scenario
autonumber
actor User
participant "Browser" as UI
participant "Active API request" as Work
participant "Cancellation API request" as Cancel
participant "JOBS + Event" as Jobs
participant "LLM HTTP response /\nASR or TTS subprocess" as Resource
UI ->> Work : Start task (task ID, request ID)
Work -> Jobs : Register owner=(user.pk, session_key, task)
Work -> Resource : Begin processing
User -> UI : Stop / close / applicable navigation
UI -> UI : Abort local controller; stop recording / playback
UI -> Cancel : POST /docpup/cancel/ with same task
Cancel -> Cancel : Require login, POST and valid task identifier
Cancel -> Jobs : Find all Events whose key[:3] equals owner
loop each matching event
  Cancel -> Jobs : event.set()
end
loop each event with an active response
  Cancel -> Resource : response.close()
end
Cancel --> UI : JSON {ok:true}
Work -> Jobs : Observe event.is_set() / event.wait()
alt ASR / TTS child still running
  Work -> Resource : kill(); wait()
else LLM streaming / extraction
  Work -> Work : Exit on cancellation or closed-response error
end
Work -> Work : finally: best-effort model unload if used
Work -> Jobs : Release acquired lock; remove request entry
Work -> Work : Close temporary directory; clear request data
Work -->> UI : Error response if connection still available
note over UI,Resource
  Cancellation is cooperative, not instantaneous rollback.
  The cancel endpoint returns success even if no matching job remains.
  Scope is a user + session + task, including multiple request IDs.
  Shared cancellation requires requests to reach the same process.
end note
@enduml
